## Linux VM corroboration

The Ubuntu VM was invoked as `limactl shell ubuntu -- bash -lc '<command>'`
after `source $HOME/.cargo/env`. It used the same three fixture channels and a
proxy-only `PATH`. `1.97.1-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu` was absent initially;
selecting it caused rustup to download that toolchain automatically. No component
was added and no crate or release tool was installed.

```text
cell   selected toolchain                         lookup fmt/clippy  rustfmt state/which  clippy state/which
neg    1.97.1-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu            0 / 0              1 / 1               1 / 1
pos    stable-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu            0 / 0              0 / 0               0 / 0
c196   1.96.0-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu            0 / 0              0 / 0               1 / 1
```

Here `lookup` is `command -v cargo-fmt cargo-clippy`; `state` is the final
status of `rustup component list --installed | grep -q`; and `which` is
`rustup which cargo-fmt` or `rustup which cargo-clippy`. The Linux result matches
the macOS matrix and the decision's claimed acquisition-keyed test behavior.

